        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-23T14:48:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just borrowed the name from apexFileForAndroidApp()\u0027s last parameter.\n\nIn \"func (a *AndroidApp) generateAndroidBuildActions()\" there is \"a.installApkName\" for this and it is used for both installDir and actual .apk filename.\n\nIn \"func (a *AndroidAppImport) generateAndroidBuildActions()\" there is no such thing but BaseModuleName() is used in installDir.\n\nOne alternative I thought about was InstallDir() which returns \"app/AppName\" part. It might be complementary to OutputFile().\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "49ad4623_6bd30d3e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 467,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 467,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f6f8c16461e74d4094af66aa90496b0badcd282c",
